{%- comment -%}
  The part-type collections, and only those. One source of truth for the two places that
  have to tell a category apart from a vehicle: the product breadcrumb, and the grouping
  on /collections.

  Why a list and not a rule: Liquid cannot see a smart collection's rule set, so it has no
  way to know that these are keyed on TYPE while the vehicle collections are keyed on TAG.
  Handle shape cannot decide it either — "body-parts" and "interior-parts" are categories,
  "ford-parts" is a vehicle, and they all end in "-parts".

  Add a category collection to content/site.json and it belongs here too, or it will be
  filed under vehicles and stop showing up as a product's category.

  Usage:
    {%- capture category_handles -%}{%- render 'category-handles' -%}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign categories = category_handles | strip | split: ',' -%}
{%- endcomment -%}
